===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|universite||institution of higher learning, body of persons constituting a university}} from {{der|en|xno|université}}, from {{der|en|fro|universitei|}}, from {{der|en|la-med|-}} stem of {{m|la|universitas}}, in juridical and {{der|en|la-lat|-}} "a number of persons associated into one body, a society, company, community, guild, corporation, etc"; in {{der|en|la|-}}, "the whole, aggregate," from {{m|la|universus||whole, entire}}. {{surf|en|universe|-ity}}.

